  "label": "creator of the image",
  "description": "The target of the meme is the person who created or edited the image, referred to as 'whoever photoshopped this'. The meme is designed to shame and blame this individual, using accusatory language and imagery. The visual metaphor of the woman being surrounded by pointing hands represents the act of being publicly targeted and criticized, which is a common trope in online shaming culture. The meme does not target a specific community or identity group based on protected characteristics, but rather any person who engages in image editing, particularly if the edit is perceived as offensive or inappropriate.",
